# setup.py's ext_modules names src/parser.c and src/scanner.c, and setuptools
# carries ext_modules SOURCES into an sdist by itself - the 0.1.3 rehearsal
# copied exactly those two and nothing else from src/. It does not carry
# HEADERS, and this extension compiles with include_dirs=["src"], so the sdist
# it produced was missing src/tree_sitter/parser.h, array.h and alloc.h and
# could not have been built by anyone who downloaded it.
#
# The npm tarball never had this problem because package.json lists "src/**" in
# files. Nothing granted the sdist the equivalent until now.
graft src
